 "title": "Welcome to Dickinson County in the beautiful state of Michigan",
 "text": "Welcome to Dickinson County in the beautiful state of Michigan\nHome\nGovernment\nCounty Services\nDickinson County Library\nDickinson County Fair\nHealth Department\nHospital Healthcare System\nRoad Commission\nConstruction Code\nFord Airport (IMT)\nVeterans Affairs\nMSU Extension\nCounty Departments\nBoard of Commissioners*\nCounty Controller\nCounty Court System\nCounty Clerk*\nRegister of Deeds*\nCounty Treasurer*\nEqualization\nSheriff's Department*\nLake Antoine Park/Campground\nDrain Commissioner*\nResidents\nLocal Area Information\nCities And Townships\nLocal Schools\nPublic Library and branches\nFor Pets and Wildlife\nRecreation\nTourist Information\nCounty Links\nCounty History Development\nCourthouse\nDemographic Information\nElected Officials\nFinancial Dashboard\nElections\nVoter Information\nEducation\nHealthCare\nSenior Citizens\nMilitary Veterans\nWelcome\nCities And Townships\nTourist Information\nRecreation\nBusiness\nCounty records information\nDemographic Information\nEmployment Opportunities\nHow Do I\nPay fines\nApply For\nAssumed Name DBAs\nBirth Certificates\nConcealed Weapons Licenses\nDeath Certificates\nDivorces\nMarriage Licenses\nEmployment Opportunities\nContact\nUseful Phone Numbers\nBoard Meeting Minutes\nRecording Documents\nFind Information On\nGo\nPrev Next\nExplore\nDickinson\nCounty\nGeographic Information System\nElections\nCalendar\nPark & Rec\nContact Us\nThank you for visiting\nDickinson County\nDickinson County looks to the future of the state and of our country as the youngest of 83 Michigan counties. It was organized from parts of Marquette , Menominee , and Iron counties by Act 89 of the Laws of 1891 of the State of Michigan. The Act was approved by the State Legislature on May 21, 1891 and took effect on October 2, 1891.\nThe county was named for Donald M. Dickinson , who served as U.S. Postmaster General under President Grover Cleveland.\nThree cities in Dickinson County: Norway became a city in 1868;\nIron Mountain was incorporated 1875; Kingsford became a village in 1923 and a city in 1947.\nThe rest of the County is governed by townships.\nBreen , Breitung , Felch , Norway , Sagola , Waucedah, West Branch\nDickinson County elected officials and government departments\nOpen hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Central time\nGet notified of meeting agendas Freedom of Information\nLive\nWork\nPlay\nLive\nWork\nPlay\nLive\nWork\nPlay\nOur government\nOur community\nOur history\nOur recreation\nCounty Departments\nBoard Of Commissioners\nCounty Controller\nCounty Clerk\nRegister Of Deeds\nCounty Treasurer\nEqualization\nCounty Departments\nSheriff's Department\nParks\nFord Airport\nProsecuting Attorney\nCourt System\nQuicklinks\nContact information\nElections\nCalendar\nParks & Rec\nBirth, Death & Marriage Records\nTaxes\nTraffic Tickets\nSmall Claims\nMeeting Minutes & Agendas\nEmployment Opportunities\nPassport Information\nCounty Committee application for public\nContact Us\n705 S. Stephenson Ave.\nIron Mountain MI 49801\nMailing Address\nPO Box 609\nIron Mountain MI 49801\npowered by revize. , The Government Website Experts. |\nLogin\n×\nImportant news for you\nOfficial Nov 3, 2026 ballot\nSpecial county board meeting Oct. 19, 2026\nRead More\nSHARE\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.dickinsoncountymi.gov/\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle Plus\nReddit\nClose",
